🔥 🎯 Bonus Task: Type-Based Processor with instanceof
You are building a processor that handles different object types differently.
📥 Input:
Object item;
⚙️ Requirements:
• Create classes Book, Movie, and Game
• Each class should have a title field
• Movie should also have an int duration
• Game should also have a String platform
• Write a method describe(Object item) that uses instanceof to:
If item is Book → return "Book: <title>" </li></title>
If item is Movie → return "Movie: <title> (</title><duration> min)" </duration>
If item is Game → return "Game: <title> [</title><platform>]" </platform>
Otherwise → return "Unknown item"
• In main, create one object of each type and print the result of describe()
📌 Constraints:
• Use only standard Java
• Output must match the required format exactly
📤 Output format:
Book: <title></title>
Movie: <title> (</title><duration> min)
Game: <title> [</title><platform>]
Unknown item</platform></duration>
📌 Test cases:
